# SokoYetu Mtaani Update Pack

This ZIP is made for your project:

`C:\Users\PC\Desktop\sokoyetu-fullstack\sokoyetu-elite-checked-fixed`

It helps you change the visible website name to **SokoYetu Mtaani** while keeping the domain **mysokoyetu.co.ke**.

## What this pack does

It adds/updates:

- Website name: `SokoYetu Mtaani`
- SEO title: `SokoYetu Mtaani | Online Shopping & Marketplace in Kenya`
- Meta description
- Open Graph social sharing tags
- Twitter card tags
- `robots.txt`
- `sitemap.xml`
- `site.webmanifest`
- A reusable brand config file

It also searches your project files and replaces common old names such as:

- `SokoYetu Marketplace Kenya`
- `SokoYetu Marketplace`
- `SokoYetu Kenya`
- `My SokoYetu`
- `Soko Yetu`
- `mysokoyetu`

## How to use in CMD

1. Unzip this ZIP.
2. Copy all extracted files into this folder:

   `C:\Users\PC\Desktop\sokoyetu-fullstack\sokoyetu-elite-checked-fixed`

3. Open CMD.
4. Run:

   ```bat
   cd C:\Users\PC\Desktop\sokoyetu-fullstack\sokoyetu-elite-checked-fixed
   apply-sokoyetu-mtaani-branding.cmd
   ```

5. Test your project locally using your usual command, for example:

   ```bat
   npm install
   npm run dev
   ```

6. If it looks good, deploy to Render:

   ```bat
   git add .
   git commit -m "Update branding to SokoYetu Mtaani"
   git push
   ```

Render should redeploy automatically if your GitHub repository is connected.

## Important

This pack does not delete your existing project files.

The script creates backup copies before editing files. Backup files end with:

`.bak-sokoyetu-mtaani`

If anything looks wrong, you can restore those backup files manually.

